      "text_raw": "A plot of the mismatch of\nthe drain current version\nweak inversion coefficient is\nshown below. This is the\nratio of the drain current to\nthe si/wi transition current\n(see Chapter 1). In terms of\nbeta, this transition current\nis about 2nb(kT/q)2 or 0.002\nb. Note that V =kT/q.\nt\nIt is clear that for weak\ninversion the spreading in\nthreshold voltage is domi-\nnant. For strong inversion,\nthe spreading in beta is\ndominant, most probably\ndue to the spreading in W and L values, whichever is smaller.",
